# 336 — R-171 batch 3: durable, host-shared tool registry (D-113, لاحق 96)
branch: m8/r171-batch3-registry-persistence   base: main dfd07311 (PR #300 merge)

## problem (main dfd07311)
tool_runtime.runtime_registry() = internal_tools.seeded_registry() -> an in-memory ToolRegistry per process.
=> under --workers N a disable in one worker does not reach the others; a restart forgets every state change + audit.

## red
pytest tests/test_r171_registry_persistence.py -> collection ERROR (ModuleNotFoundError: agent_civilization.core.tool_registry_store)

## fix
new agent_civilization/core/tool_registry_store.py: PersistentToolRegistry(ToolRegistry) on one SQLite file per host (WAL)
  reads: reload when the shared revision changed; mutations: BEGIN IMMEDIATE -> reload latest -> inherited rule -> write diff
  + audit (refusals too) + revision; failed write -> rollback + drop memory; per-row SHA-256 digest checked on load;
  seed(): one transaction, missing only, stored wins (seed_drift), tombstones honoured.
tool_runtime: uses it; any RegistryStoreError -> refusal "tool registry store unavailable" (fail-closed, no path).
  AGOS_DISABLED_TOOLS written once and durable (re-enable via the CLI).
new scripts/tool_registry_admin.py: list | disable | enable | audit (--actor required for changes).
tests/conftest.py: per-test store file (AGOS_TOOL_REGISTRY_DB), removed after the test.
tool_registry.py: docstring points to the persistent variant (no rule changed).

## green
tests/test_r171_registry_persistence.py -> 15 passed (real subprocesses for sharing / stale-mutation / 6-process concurrency / env / CLI)
with r171 batch 1+2 + r160 log redaction -> 99 passed

## mutations (each restored; files cmp-identical afterwards)   [persistence + gate tests, 29]
_sync never reloads after first load          -> 3 failed
no reload inside the mutation transaction     -> 3 failed
no memory drop after a failed write           -> 1 failed
seed drift detection disabled                 -> 1 failed
row digest check removed                      -> 1 failed
env disable written by every worker           -> 1 failed
store error -> allow (fail-open)              -> 3 failed

## cost
check("analyst") ~5.8 us; check("self_developer") ~51.9 us (9 tools) — one indexed SELECT per registry read.

## full suite (local)
1st run: 1 failed, 3798 passed, 8 skipped, 17 deselected, 9 xfailed in 541.20s
  FAILED test_r160_g159_1_log_redaction::test_scanner_finds_no_unreviewed_raw_exception_log_in_runtime_code
  cause: tool_runtime logged the raw RegistryStoreError. fix: RegistryStoreError.reason (closed vocabulary) is logged
  instead, with a REVIEWED entry in scripts/scan_raw_exception_logs.py (precedent: sse.StreamLimit.reason).
  scan: flagged=4 reviewed=4 unreviewed=0 stale_reviewed=0; affected tests re-run: 99 passed.

## declared limits
host-local (multi-host = deployment decision: Postgres/Supabase or Redis); audit grows without rotation and is loaded
in memory; whoever can write the file controls the registry (digest is not a signature); no API; no health checker;
not a sandbox / permission system (R-172).

